# TIQCollect — ignore rules.
#
# 2026-08-17: this file used to say the platform-wide basics (.env, .venv/,
# node_modules/, __pycache__/, dist/) "are already covered by ../.gitignore".
# That was true while this lived inside the Collections monorepo as
# field-ops-stub/. It is now a standalone repo, so ../.gitignore is gone and
# nothing was ignoring any of them — backend/.env, holding live Postgres/MinIO/
# Twilio credentials, was showing up as a stageable untracked file. Those rules
# are therefore inlined below.

# ── Env / secrets (NEVER commit real keys) ──────────────────────────────────
# Anything ending .env at any depth is local-only; only .example templates ship.
.env
.env.*
**/*.env
firebase-credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# ── Python tooling caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# ── Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.local

# ── Data & uploads ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
backend/data/incoming/

# ── Logs / temp ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
tmp/

# ── Docker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker-compose.override.yml

# ── OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Re-includes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Negations must come AFTER the rules they override — gitignore takes the last
# matching rule, so these would be dead if they sat above the .env block.
!*.example
!**/*.example

# Postgres dumps taken before/after a destructive reseed. Binary, large,
# and regenerable from scripts/seed_data.py — never in git.
backups/

# ── Synthetic-experiment artifacts (2026-09-03) ─────────────────────────────
# scripts/run_synthetic_experiment.py writes a simulated collections book to a
# SEPARATE database and drops two artifacts here. Neither belongs in git:
#
#   ground_truth.json  the simulator's hidden borrower/agent variables. It is
#                      regenerable from --seed, and committing it would put a
#                      file full of "true" repayment propensities next to the
#                      feature code — exactly the thing that must never become
#                      a feature.
#   *.csv              exported training frames; regenerable, and large.
backend/data/synthetic/
backend/data/*.csv
backend/app/ml/models/*.json

# ── Modelling panel (2026-09-08) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/build_modelling_dataset.py writes a 120k-row synthetic panel plus the
# simulator's latent variables. Neither belongs in git: the panel is fully
# regenerable from the seed recorded in its own dataset_metadata.json, and
# ground_truth.json holds the true repayment propensities the model is supposed
# to infer — a file of answers sitting next to the feature code.
#
# The ARTIFACTS built from it (backend/app/ml/artifacts/) are deliberately NOT
# ignored. The model, its metrics, its EDA and its model document are the
# deliverable, and app/ml/models/*.json above is already an object lesson in
# what happens when a result is written somewhere git cannot see it.
backend/data/modelling/

# The EVENT LEDGER and its derived panel (2026-09-09).
# scripts/build_ledger_dataset.py writes an append-only event ledger plus the
# panel derived from it — ~100k account-months and ~340k events at the full
# tier. Regenerable from the seed and intercept recorded in its own
# dataset_metadata.json, so it is data, not a deliverable. Same reasoning as
# the modelling panel above.
#
# REALISM_REPORT.txt is deliberately covered too: it is a measurement OF a
# generated dataset, so a committed copy would drift from whatever the
# generator currently produces — the exact trap ml/models/*.json already is.
backend/data/ledger/

# Simulator acceptance run output (frontend/e2e/simulator_acceptance.py)
frontend/e2e/screenshots/

# Rollback manifests written by the demo operator scripts (demo_record_*, ptp_lifecycle_backfill).
# Runtime output of a data change, kept with the deployment, not in git.
backend/docs/rollback/

# Production database dumps (docker-compose.prod.yml mounts ./backups).
backups/
